Now let $F(x,p)$ be any classical observable. The chain rule gives $\begin{aligned}
  \frac{dF}{dt}
  &=
  \frac{\partial F}{\partial x}\dot x
  +\frac{\partial F}{\partial p}\dot p\\
  &=
  \frac{\partial F}{\partial x}
  \frac{\partial H}{\partial p}
  -
  \frac{\partial F}{\partial p}
  \frac{\partial H}{\partial x}.
  \end{aligned}$ The combination on the right is the Poisson bracket: $\{F,H\}_{\mathrm{PB}}
  =
  \frac{\partial F}{\partial x}
  \frac{\partial H}{\partial p}
  -
  \frac{\partial F}{\partial p}
  \frac{\partial H}{\partial x}.$ Thus $\boxed{\frac{dF}{dt}=\{F,H\}_{\mathrm{PB}}.}$

