Suppose that after an elapsed time $T$, $\ket{A}\longmapsto\hat U(T)\ket{A},
  \qquad
  \ket{B}\longmapsto\hat U(T)\ket{B}.$ The corresponding transformed bra is $\bra{B}\longmapsto\bra{B}\hat U^\dagger(T).$ Preservation of the inner product requires $\begin{aligned}
  \braket{B}{A}
  &=
  \bra{B}\hat U^\dagger(T)\hat U(T)\ket{A}.\end{aligned}$ This must hold for every pair $\ket A,\ket B$. Therefore $\boxed{\hat U^\dagger(T)\hat U(T)=\mathbf 1.}$ In finite dimensions this also implies $\hat U(T)\hat U^\dagger(T)=\mathbf1$. The evolution operator is unitary.

