p.src:
Writing the state at an arbitrary initial time $t$, the evolution law is $\ket{\psi(t+T)}
  =
  \hat U(T)\ket{\psi(t)}.$ No elapsed time means no change, $\hat U(0)=\mathbf1.$ Successive intervals compose: $\hat U(T_2)\hat U(T_1)=\hat U(T_1+T_2)$ when the Hamiltonian has no explicit time dependence. This is why a long evolution can be assembled from many short steps.

