p.src:
Apply Equation  to a state: $\ket{\psi(t+\epsilon)}
  =
  \left(
    \mathbf1-\frac{i\epsilon}{\hbar}\hat H
  \right)
  \ket{\psi(t)}
  +O(\epsilon^2).$ Subtract $\ket{\psi(t)}$, divide by $\epsilon$, and take $\epsilon\to0$: $\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\ket{\psi(t)}
  =
  -\frac{i}{\hbar}\hat H\ket{\psi(t)}.$ Multiplication by $i\hbar$ gives $\boxed{
  i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\ket{\psi(t)}
  =
  \hat H\ket{\psi(t)}.}$

