A general polarization state is $\ket{\psi(t)}
  =
  \alpha(t)\ket{x}+\beta(t)\ket{y}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha(t)\\
    \beta(t)
  \end{pmatrix}.$ The probabilities of obtaining $x$ and $y$ polarization are $|\alpha(t)|^2$ and $|\beta(t)|^2$.

