p.src:
The Schrödinger equation becomes $i\hbar
  \frac{d}{dt}
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha\\
    \beta
  \end{pmatrix}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    E_1&0\\
    0&E_2
  \end{pmatrix}
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha\\
    \beta
  \end{pmatrix}.$ The two component equations decouple: $i\hbar\dot\alpha=E_1\alpha,
  \qquad
  i\hbar\dot\beta=E_2\beta.$ Their solutions are $\alpha(t)=\alpha(0)e^{-iE_1t/\hbar},
  \qquad
  \beta(t)=\beta(0)e^{-iE_2t/\hbar}.$ Thus $\ket{\psi(t)}
  =
  \begin{pmatrix}
    \alpha(0)e^{-iE_1t/\hbar}\\
    \beta(0)e^{-iE_2t/\hbar}
  \end{pmatrix}.$

