p.src:
Prepare the photon with a first $+45^\circ$ polarizer. Then $\alpha(0)=\beta(0)=\frac{1}{\sqrt2},$ and $\mathcal A_+(t)
  =
  \frac12
  \left(
    e^{-iE_1t/\hbar}
    +e^{-iE_2t/\hbar}
  \right).$ The transmission probability is the absolute square: $\begin{aligned}
  P_+(t)
  &=
  |\mathcal A_+(t)|^2\\
  &=
  \frac14
  \left(
    e^{-iE_1t/\hbar}
    +e^{-iE_2t/\hbar}
  \right)
  \left(
    e^{iE_1t/\hbar}
    +e^{iE_2t/\hbar}
  \right)\\
  &=
  \frac14
  \left[
    2
    +e^{i(E_2-E_1)t/\hbar}
    +e^{-i(E_2-E_1)t/\hbar}
  \right].
  \end{aligned}$

