Let $\hat K$ be a fixed observable with no explicit time dependence. Its expectation value in the evolving state is $\expect{\hat K}
  =
  \bra{\psi(t)}\hat K\ket{\psi(t)}.$ Only the bra and ket vary. The product rule gives $\frac{d}{dt}\expect{\hat K}
  =
  \bra{\dot\psi}\hat K\ket{\psi}
  +
  \bra{\psi}\hat K\ket{\dot\psi}.$

