p.src:
Substitution gives $\begin{aligned}
  \frac{d}{dt}\expect{\hat K}
  &=
  \frac{i}{\hbar}
  \bra{\psi}\hat H\hat K\ket{\psi}
  -
  \frac{i}{\hbar}
  \bra{\psi}\hat K\hat H\ket{\psi}\\
  &=
  \frac{i}{\hbar}
  \expect{[\hat H,\hat K]}\\
  &=
  -\frac{i}{\hbar}
  \expect{[\hat K,\hat H]}.
  \end{aligned}$

