Look for a solution that remains a momentum eigenstate: $\psi_p(x,t)
  =
  f(t)e^{ipx/\hbar}.$ The number $p$ is the momentum eigenvalue, because $-i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial x}
  e^{ipx/\hbar}
  =
  p\,e^{ipx/\hbar}.$ The function $f(t)$ is a spectator under spatial differentiation and contains all time dependence.

